# ToastStack / ToastRow — more than one transient confirmation on screen at
# once, without them landing in the same spot and overlapping. `ui/Toast`
# already draws ONE such message, pinned to the corner; a page that can raise
# two at once (a like confirmation while a save is still failing, say) has
# nowhere for the second one to go, because `ui/Toast`'s own `.x-toast` is
# `position: fixed` to the exact same spot every time. `ToastStack` is the one
# `position: fixed` container, and `ToastRow` is the same pill un-pinned from
# the viewport so several can stack inside it.
#
#     use ToastStack():
#         if justFollowed:
#             use ToastRow("ok", "Followed")
#         if failed(save) != "":
#             use ToastRow("danger", failed(save))
#
# ── AUTO-DISMISS IS NOT HERE, AND IT IS A REAL GAP ────────────────────────────
#
# The identical gap `ui/toast.fct`'s own doc comment already names for a single
# toast: dismissal needs something to flip a cell after N seconds with no
# further input, and this language has no timer — CATALOG.md's own "what
# still needs the language" list carries it as item 2, `after 5s: cell =
# false`. So, exactly like `ui/Toast`, each `ToastRow` is a *derived* view of a
# condition the host already tracks (`justFollowed`, `failed(save) != ""`) and
# stays up for exactly as long as that condition holds — which is honest, and
# not a substitute for the timer this would use once the language has one.
#
# ── WHY THIS DOES NOT IMPORT `ui/toast.fct` ───────────────────────────────────
#
# `Toast`'s own `.x-toast` carries `position: fixed` on the SAME element that
# holds its tone colour and its mark, so nesting several of them inside a
# stacking container would still plant each one at the bottom-centre of the
# viewport rather than in the stack. The tone vocabulary is small enough
# (three lines of `match`) that `ui/toast.fct`'s own note about `Toast`/`Tag`
# applies here too — "they ship their own constants" rather than importing a
# vocabulary file for three colours — so this file spells its own, scoped to
# `.x-toastrow`, rather than fighting `ui/toast.fct`'s positioning to reuse it.
app FacetNotify:
    css:
        [data-fa-mount] .x-toaststack { position: fixed; bottom: 24px; left: 50%;
                       transform: translateX(-50%); z-index: 60; display: flex;
                       flex-direction: column-reverse; align-items: stretch; gap: 10px;
                       width: min(90vw, 420px); border: none; background: none; padding: 0; }
        [data-fa-mount] .x-toastrow { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px;
                       box-sizing: border-box; padding: 12px 16px; border-radius: 12px;
                       font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.35; box-shadow: 0 8px 28px rgba(0,0,0,.45);
                       background: var(--x-panel, #16181c); color: var(--fa-fg);
                       border: 1px solid var(--x-line, #2f3336); }
        [data-fa-mount] .x-toastrow-ok { border-color: #00ba7c; }
        [data-fa-mount] .x-toastrow-warn { border-color: #ffd400; }
        [data-fa-mount] .x-toastrow-danger { border-color: #f4212e; }
        [data-fa-mount] .x-toastrow-mark { font-size: 15px; }
        [data-fa-mount] .x-toaststack > div:empty:not([class]) { display: none; }
    component ToastStack():
        box class "x-toaststack":
            slot
    component ToastRow(tone: text, message: text):
        match tone:
            case "ok":
                row class "x-toastrow x-toastrow-ok":
                    text "✓" class "x-toastrow-mark"
                    text "{message}"
            case "warn":
                row class "x-toastrow x-toastrow-warn":
                    text "!" class "x-toastrow-mark"
                    text "{message}"
            case "danger":
                row class "x-toastrow x-toastrow-danger":
                    text "✕" class "x-toastrow-mark"
                    text "{message}"
            else:
                row class "x-toastrow":
                    text "{message}"
